  "tldr": [
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/ai",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Languages as designed latent spaces",
      "url": "https://blog.jsbarretto.com/post/languages-as-latent-spaces",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/ljg2qr",
      "score": 8,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "intarga",
      "published": "2026-07-25T15:13:27Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Human and programming languages function as discrete, engineered representations mapping complex semantic concepts into structured symbolic abstractions.",
        "LLMs convert discrete syntax into continuous vector latent spaces, enabling geometric semantic alignment and cross-domain representation.",
        "Designing domain-specific languages (DSLs) and structured prompts offers explicit control over an AI model's internal latent space traversal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "A shell colon does nothing. Use it anyway",
      "url": "https://refp.se/articles/your-shell-and-the-magic-colon",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/eidh3u",
      "score": 98,
      "comments": 39,
      "author": "refp",
      "published": "2026-07-25T11:33:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "The POSIX shell colon (\":\") is a built-in no-op returning exit code 0, commonly replacing \"true\" in performance-sensitive infinite loops.",
        "Combined with parameter expansion, \":\" evaluates side effects like default variable assignment (\":${VAR:=default}\") without spawning subshells or executing external binaries.",
        "It functions as a zero-cost syntactic placeholder in empty conditional blocks and enables multi-line comments using heredocs (\": <<'EOF'\")."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Exploiting Volvo/Eicher's fleet platform to gain control over all users/vehicles",
      "url": "https://eaton-works.com/2026/07/27/my-eicher-hack/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49070756",
      "score": 161,
      "comments": 54,
      "author": "EatonZ",
      "published": "2026-07-27T15:08:16Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Critical API vulnerabilities in Volvo/Eicher telematics platforms allowed unauthenticated account takeover and full administrative access across user fleets.",
        "Exploitation granted remote access to vehicle telematics data, real-time GPS tracking, and potentially unsafe direct vehicle command execution.",
        "Highlighting heavy-vehicle IoT risks, automotive platforms must enforce strict API authorization (BOLA prevention) and isolate telematics control channels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "rss",
      "subsource": "aws.amazon.com",
      "category": "devops",
      "title": "Amazon Neptune now supports tag-based access control for IAM",
      "url": "https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-neptune-tbac/",
      "discuss_url": "https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-neptune-tbac/",
      "score": null,
      "comments": null,
      "author": "aws@amazon.com",
      "published": "2026-07-27T22:00:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Amazon Neptune now supports IAM Tag-Based Access Control (TBAC), dynamically authorizing neptune-db:* data-plane actions using resource and principal tags.",
        "IAM policies and SCPs can leverage SAML or OIDC session tags to govern access without manually enumerating individual cluster ARNs.",
        "TBAC mitigates lateral access risks in shared VPCs while enabling granular permissions like neptune-db:QueryLanguage for dynamic multi-tenant isolation."
      ]
    },
